927
00:27:45,020 --> 00:27:47,460
In fact, it will not cause any effect at all.

928
00:27:47,460 --> 00:27:48,040
Right?

929
00:27:48,040 --> 00:27:50,200
So this second step,

930
00:27:50,200 --> 00:27:52,340
in effect, does nothing at all.

931
00:27:52,340 --> 00:27:54,060
What we care about is here,

932
00:27:54,060 --> 00:27:55,420
conversely, we care about its first step.

933
00:27:55,420 --> 00:27:57,760
Now, what this step actually achieves

934
00:27:57,760 --> 00:28:00,120
is that it takes the value in the CSR register,

935
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:01,020
reads it out,

936
00:28:01,020 --> 00:28:02,720
and puts it into rd.

937
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:04,380
That's exactly the effect we get.

938
00:28:04,380 --> 00:28:06,620
So we often use this instruction

939
00:28:06,620 --> 00:28:10,220
to implement read operations on CSR instructions.

